{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor avoided substituting online judgment for the surgical/anesthesia team, actively queried/asked for records, and repeatedly converted medication, wound, thrombosis, fall, rehab, and red-flag risks into executable caregiver actions. No responsibility-chain error is evident: key uncertainties were carried forward to named owners/times, medication changes were tied to formal orders, and the family repeatedly demonstrated receipt. High-order credit is earned for correcting ambiguity about bone findings/surgical clearance, repairing the “move vs stay in bed” conflict into team-based rules, and achieving safe bounded closure with residual follow-up tasks. This supports a Perfect grade.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00736",
        "explanation": "The doctor gives an executable home-observation plan and urgent escalation boundaries near the end of the trajectory.",
        "quote": "可以，今晚按交接纸居家观察。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00736",
        "explanation": "The closure carries medication, wound, mobility, and red-flag instructions forward without pretending all follow-up is complete.",
        "quote": "药按已确认的时间和疗程服，不自行改动；"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode is safely closed for current home care after surgery, dressing checks, medication confirmation, and follow-up scheduling. Remaining uncertainties such as future 4–6 week visit logistics are nonblocking and assigned to routine confirmation, while urgent red flags have clear action paths.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
